      <h2>About Mnarani Marine Turtle Pond</h2>
      <div>Mnarani Marine Turtle Pond in Nungwi is a natural lagoon connected to the ocean where endangered hawksbill and green sea turtles are protected, rehabilitated, and released. Visitors can observe turtles at different life stages from hatchlings to adults, learn about turtle biology and conservation challenges, and witness scheduled feeding sessions. The project, run by local conservationists, also conducts beach patrols to protect nesting sites. All visits support the project's rescue, rehabilitation, and community education programs.</div>
